hadiths[3]{hadithnumber,text}:
"15506","Waki narrated to us, he said: Sufyan informed us, and Abd al-Rahman, from Sufyan, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, he said: And Nafi ibn Jubayr ibn Mutim said, from Bishr ibn Suhaym, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) addressed on the day of al-Tashriq, Abd al-Rahman said: In the days of Hajj, and said: None shall enter Paradise except a Muslim soul, and these days are days of eating and drinking."
"15507","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Nafi ibn Jubayr ibn Mutim, from a man of the Companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he sent Bishr ibn Suhaym and ordered him to announce: Verily none shall enter Paradise except a believing soul, and they are days of eating and drinking, meaning the days of al-Tashriq."
"15508","Bahz narrated to us: Shubah narrated to us, he said: Habib ibn Abi Thabit informed me that he heard Nafi ibn Jubayr ibn Mutim narrating from a man of the Companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called Bishr ibn Suhaym, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) addressed and said: None shall enter Paradise except a believer, and these days are days of eating and drinking."
